on</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Diagnose and develop care plans using Expressable’s clinical tools and platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deliver outcomes-focused care with an emphasis on caregiver engagement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Complete all documentation accurately and on time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in required training and team communication</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide coverage for PTO and sick leave to ensure care continuity</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>⭐ Requirements:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Master’s or Doctorate degree in Occupational Therapy (MOT, OTD, or equivalent) and individual NPI number</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Licensed in a key state (or willingness to obtain prior to start date)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and comfort with teletherapy platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Minimum 2 years of post-graduate experience in pediatric settings</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong computer literacy and ability to learn new systems independently</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with insurance-based or Medicaid populations</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#LI-VZ1</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">#ZR</p>","descriptionPlain":"W2 employment  |  $40 - $54/hour |  Flexible Scheduling\n\n(This role is primarily remote; however, hybrid opportunities may be available in certain markets. Candidates must hold a Virginia state license and ideally be located within Virginia.)\n\nWelcome to Expressable! We’re an SLP-founded company on a mission to expand access to family-led online therapy. We believe in empowering caregivers to be active participants in their loved one’s communication journey, and are proud to be backed by 3,500+ 5-star reviews.\n\n⭐ Compensation:\nThis is a non-exempt, W2 hourly position.\n\n - Clinical rate: $40-$54/hour: Covers both direct sessions and documentation time.\n\n\n\n⭐ Schedule and flexibility: \nDesign your own schedule around your needs and lifestyle. Our clients typically seek services after 3:30pm weekdays and early mornings/afternoons on weekends. A minimum of 7 hours of total availability per week is required.\n\n\n\n⭐ Why OTs choose Expressable:\n\n - AI-assisted documentation: Our clinician-built AI assistant, Scout, dramatically cuts documentation time and admin tasks\n\n - Part-time benefit eligibility: 401(k) matching, sick time, Employee Assistance Program\n\n - Growth opportunities: Expressable has ample opportunities for professional development and positions to grow your career\n\n - Tons of free resources: Approved CEUs, library of home programs and exercises, access to virtual materials, and much more\n\n - Company-provided hardware: A new Macbook + iPad for clinical care\n\n - Dedicated support teams: Specialized team for patient insurance, billing, authorizations, and more so you can focus on care\n\n - Vibrant community 250+ strong: Join a collaborative team of clinicians committed to transforming speech therapy\n\n\n\n⭐What you’ll do:\n\n - Provide remote occupational therapy sessions/evaluations for a diverse pediatric population\n\n - Diagnose and develop care plans using Expressable’s clinical tools and platform\n\n - Deliver outcomes-focused care with an emphasis on caregiver engagement\n\n - Complete all documentation accurately and on time\n\n - Participate in required training and team communication\n\n - Provide coverage for PTO and sick leave to ensure care continuity\n\n\n\n⭐ Requirements:\n\n - Master’s or Doctorate degree in Occupational Therapy (MOT, OTD, or equivalent) and individual NPI number\n\n - Licensed in a key state (or willingness to obtain prior to start date)\n\n - Reliable internet connection and comfort with teletherapy platforms\n\n - Minimum 2 years of post-graduate experience in pediatric settings\n\n - Strong computer literacy and ability to learn new systems independently\n\n - Familiarity with insurance-based or Medicaid populations\n\n\n\n#LI-VZ1\n\n#ZR","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$40 – $54 per hour","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"2cec13d6-fefb-4e34-81c4-53bf691f32be","tierSummary":"$40 – $54 per hour","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"25506315-3cf7-4cff-9fb8-db0f2286c4fc","summary":"$40 – $54 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":40,"maxValue":54}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":40,"maxValue":54}]}},{"id":"36d87a9a-5bca-492d-9be6-f5ebc4554b02","title":"Payer Compliance Specialist","department":"Payor and Revenue Operations","team":"Payor and Revenue Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T16:52:54.702+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"USA","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"USA"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/expressable/36d87a9a-5bca-492d-9be6-f5ebc4554b02","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/expressable/36d87a9a-5bca-492d-9be6-f5ebc4554b02/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Title: </strong>Payer Compliance Specialist<strong><br />Location: </strong>100% Remote (anywhere in the US)<strong><br />Status: </strong>Full-Time Non-Exempt | Direct Hire<strong><br /> Pay: </strong>$24.00 - $27.00 per hour</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong><br /></strong>We're a fast-growing, fully remote organization on a mission to make a real difference — and we know our people make that possible. As we scale, we're adding a high-ownership, high-impact role to our team. We're seeking a Payer Compliance Specialist who will manage payer setup and policy updates while supporting internal training, clean claims, and cross-functional compliance projects.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Expressable</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expressable is a virtual speech therapy practice on a mission to transform care delivery and expand access to high-quality services, serving thousands of clients since our inception in late 2019. We are passionate advocates of parent-focused intervention. Our e-learning platform contains thousands of home-based learning modules authored by our clinical team, helping SLPs empower caregivers to integrate speech therapy techniques into their child’s daily life and improve outcomes. Our mission is to set a new standard in speech therapy by making every caregiver a champion of their loved one’s success. We envision a world where everyone can fulfill their communication potential.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You Would Be Doing</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.</em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain payer setup and readiness including fee schedules, EFT/ERA configuration, portal access, and payer profile updates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interpret payer contracts and manuals to extract operational requirements and support clean claim submission.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor payer updates and policy changes, assess their impact, and assist with implementation and compliance tracking; attending new payer orientation meetings and ongoing payer training sessions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support audit and compliance efforts by assisting with external payer responses, conducting internal reviews, and ensuring required training is completed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain up-to-date reference materials and serve as a resource to internal teams on payer rules and workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally on special projects to improve payer compliance, documentation, and training systems.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You Bring to Expressable</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Education and Experience</em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Associate's or Bachelor's degree in healthcare administration, business, or a related field (or equivalent work experience).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience in medical billing, revenue cycle operations, payer compliance, or healthcare auditing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working within a healthcare setting is required.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with payer contracts, reimbursement policies, and healthcare documentation standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical Billing/Coding Certification not required, but a plus.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Technical Skills</em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with practice management systems, payer portals, and claims processing tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing EFT/ERA setup, fee schedules, and provider enrollment data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong spreadsheet and document management skills (e.g., Google Workspace or Microsoft Office).</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Core Competencies</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>In addition to the competencies associated with our core values, the Contract Coordinator should bring the following:</em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Detail-oriented with excellent organizational and follow-through abilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and critical thinking skills to interpret payer policies and identify operational impacts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effective verbal and written communication skills, including the ability to deliver training and simplify complex topics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to collaborate cross-functionally with billing, clinical, and compliance teams in a fully remote environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adaptability to evolving payer requirements and healthcare regulations.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Join Us?</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional paid time off policies that encourage and support life balance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401k matching to ensure our staff have what they need to enjoy their retirement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Health insurance options that ensure well-being for the whole person and their family</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Company paid life, short-term disability, and long-term disability coverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A remote work environment that strives for connectivity through professional collaboration and personal connection</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Work Authorization</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are interested in every qualified candidate who is eligible to work in the United States. However, we are not able to sponsor visas at this time.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>More about Expressable</strong><br />Expressable values people. From the technology we develop, the services we provide, and the culture we maintain, Expressable cares about the experience of our employees, clients, and prospects. We intentionally create and sustain supportive environments in which everyone - clients, caregivers, speech-language pathologists, and team members - can achieve their highest potential.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that building trusting and collaborative relationships is paramount to delivering quality care so we operate with the highest levels of honesty, transparency, and accountability as individuals and a collaborative team. We believe that transforming therapy happens through the steady and iterative problem solving of an interdisciplinary team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expressable is an equal opportunity workplace. We celebrate and embrace diversity and are committed to building a team that represents a broad tapestry of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expressable is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. In keeping with our commitment, Expressable will take the steps to ensure people with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodations. Accordingly, if reasonable accommodation is required to fully participate in the job application or interview process, to perform the essential functions of the position, and/or to receive all other benefits and privileges of employment, please contact us at hr@expressable.io.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>E-Verify</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all person hired to work in the United States. Expressable participates in E-Verify.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://e-verify.uscis.gov/web/media/resourcesContents/E-Verify_Participation_Poster_ES.pdf\"><u>E-Verify Participation Poster</u></a></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.everify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf\"><u>E-Verify Right to Work Poster</u></a></p>","descriptionPlain":"Job Title: Payer Compliance Specialist\nLocation: 100% Remote (anywhere in the US)\nStatus: Full-Time Non-Exempt | Direct Hire\n Pay: $24.00 - $27.00 per hour\n\n\nWe're a fast-growing, fully remote organization on a mission to make a real difference — and we know our people make that possible. As we scale, we're adding a high-ownership, high-impact role to our team. We're seeking a Payer Compliance Specialist who will manage payer setup and policy updates while supporting internal training, clean claims, and cross-functional compliance projects.\n\nAbout Expressable\n\nExpressable is a virtual speech therapy practice on a mission to transform care delivery and expand access to high-quality services, serving thousands of clients since our inception in late 2019. We are passionate advocates of parent-focused intervention. Our e-learning platform contains thousands of home-based learning modules authored by our clinical team, helping SLPs empower caregivers to integrate speech therapy techniques into their child’s daily life and improve outcomes. Our mission is to set a new standard in speech therapy by making every caregiver a champion of their loved one’s success. We envision a world where everyone can fulfill their communication potential.\n\nWhat You Would Be Doing\n\nReasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.\n\n - Maintain payer setup and readiness including fee schedules, EFT/ERA configuration, portal access, and payer profile updates.\n\n - Interpret payer contracts and manuals to extract operational requirements and support clean claim submission.\n\n - Monitor payer updates and policy changes, assess their impact, and assist with implementation and compliance tracking; attending new payer orientation meetings and ongoing payer training sessions.\n\n - Support audit and compliance efforts by assisting with external payer responses, conducting internal reviews, and ensuring required training is completed.\n\n - Maintain up-to-date reference materials and serve as a resource to internal teams on payer rules and workflows.\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally on special projects to improve payer compliance, documentation, and training systems.\n\nWhat You Bring to Expressable\n\nEducation and Experience\n\n - Associate's or Bachelor's degree in healthcare administration, business, or a related field (or equivalent work experience).\n\n - 3+ years of experience in medical billing, revenue cycle operations, payer compliance, or healthcare auditing.\n\n - Experience working within a healthcare setting is required.\n\n - Familiarity with payer contracts, reimbursement policies, and healthcare documentation standards.\n\n - Medical Billing/Coding Certification not required, but a plus.\n\nTechnical Skills\n\n - Proficiency with practice management systems, payer portals, and claims processing tools.\n\n - Experience managing EFT/ERA setup, fee schedules, and provider enrollment data.\n\n - Strong spreadsheet and document management skills (e.g., Google Workspace or Microsoft Office).\n\nCore Competencies\n\nIn addition to the competencies associated with our core values, the Contract Coordinator should bring the following:\n\n - Detail-oriented with excellent organizational and follow-through abilities.\n\n - Strong analytical and critical thinking skills to interpret payer policies and identify operational impacts.\n\n - Effective verbal and written communication skills, including the ability to deliver training and simplify complex topics.\n\n - Ability to collaborate cross-functionally with billing, clinical, and compliance teams in a fully remote environment.\n\n - Adaptability to evolving payer requirements and healthcare regulations.\n\nWhy Join Us?\n\n - Exceptional paid time off policies that encourage and support life balance\n\n - 401k matching to ensure our staff have what they need to enjoy their retirement\n\n - Health insurance options that ensure well-being for the whole person and their family\n\n - Company paid life, short-term disability, and long-term disability coverage\n\n - A remote work environment that strives for connectivity through professional collaboration and personal connection\n\nWork Authorization\n\nWe are interested in every qualified candidate who is eligible to work in the United States. However, we are not able to sponsor visas at this time.\n\n\nMore about Expressable\nExpressable values people. From the technology we develop, the services we provide, and the culture we maintain, Expressable cares about the experience of our employees, clients, and prospects. We intentionally create and sustain supportive environments in which everyone - clients, caregivers, speech-language pathologists, and team members - can achieve their highest potential.\n\nWe believe that building trusting and collaborative relationships is paramount to delivering quality care so we operate with the highest levels of honesty, transparency, and accountability as individuals and a collaborative team. We believe that transforming therapy happens through the steady and iterative problem solving of an interdisciplinary team.\n\nExpressable is an equal opportunity workplace. We celebrate and embrace diversity and are committed to building a team that represents a broad tapestry of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills.\n\nExpressable is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. In keeping with our commitment, Expressable will take the steps to ensure people with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodations. Accordingly, if reasonable accommodation is required to fully participate in the job application or interview process, to perform the essential functions of the position, and/or to receive all other benefits and privileges of employment, please contact us at hr@expressable.io.\n\n\nE-Verify\n\nFederal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all person hired to work in the United States. Expressable participates in E-Verify.\n\nE-Verify Participation Poster https://e-verify.uscis.gov/web/media/resourcesContents/E-Verify_Participation_Poster_ES.pdf\n\nE-Verify Right to Work Poster https://www.everify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$24 – $27 per hour","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"20fb0156-bb5e-45bf-8a02-34a8aae1dc9c","tierSummary":"$24 – $27 per hour","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"cd078677-509b-4c15-b5a9-90fc87a6c9d2","summary":"$24 – $27 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":24,"maxValue":27}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":24,"maxValue":27}]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}